    "\"All Saints'\" (Redding, Jan 4) and \"All Saints' Memorial\" (Sacramento, Jan 11) are two distinct congregations, transcribed as printed, not a duplicate.",
    "\"Grace Church\" appears twice for three different towns across the year (St. Helena and Wheatland, and again later as Fairfield on a separate date) and \"Holy Trinity\" appears three times (Willows, Ukiah, Nevada City) -- the diocese's own shared/generic congregation names recurring at different towns, not an error, transcribed as printed each time.",
    "Two church names wrap across multiple lines in the source's own table layout and are reassembled as printed: \"Belfry Episcopal & Lutheran Campus Ministry\" (Jan 18) and \"St. Augustine of Canterbury\" (Aug 16, Rocklin). Likewise the city \"Mount Shasta\" (Aug 23, St. Barnabas') wraps across two lines in the source (\"Mount\" / \"Shasta\") and is reassembled as one place name. All reassembled by rendering the source PDF's own page images and visually confirming the pairing of church name to city against the table's row boundaries, not by trusting the linearized text extraction alone, per this corpus's standing rule for layouts with wrapped/multi-line cells.",
    "Every date in the source falls on a Sunday of 2026, confirmed by calendar arithmetic against the ISO dates transcribed."
